               3                     !
               4                     !          a bicubic spline interpolator to interpolate from a grid
               5                     !          with constant i (first dimension) grid spacing and variable
               6                     !          k (second dimension) grid spacing to a grid with
               7                     !          variable grid spacing. all grids are assumed to have point
               8                     !          (i,1) in the upper left corner with i increasing to the right
               9                     !          and k increasing downward.
              10                     !
              11                     ! **** input ****
              12                     !
              13                     !  nx: no. of points in e-w direction of input arrays
              14                     !  my: no. of points in n-s direction of input arrays
              15                     !  lev: no. of levels in input arrays
              16                     !  lpout: no. of levels in output arrays
              17                     !  pk: independent interpolation variable for input grid
              18                     !  pklp: indepentdent inter var appended to bottom of pk array
              19                     !  ff: dependent variable for input grid
              20                     !  flp: bottom boundary condition of f, defined at pklp
              21                     !  pkout: independent interpolation variable for output grid
              22                     !  tensy: cubic spline tension factor.
              23                     !
              24                     ! **** output ****
              25                     !
              26                     !  t: dependent variable on output grid
              27                     !
